    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The school of study is an Advanced Bridge into Health, Life Sciences, and other STEM-aligned fields, with. The Hub is in its second year and serves 50 high school students who travel to Mission Bay for half of their school day. As part of my 2023-2024 POLS Field Project I conducted a qualitative analysis of the school’s current program. I interviewed 20 students, 5 partner site members, and two instructional staff members. Using coding and trend analysis, in my program report I outlined strengths and opportunities according to the school’s Design Principles and other emerging themes that developed naturally from the research. There is no summary of findings in the program report because it is designed to facilitate the school’s internal ability to create their own takeaways and action items. My research and analysis provides the school leadership with tools to effectively develop their systems and offerings as they scale their program to over 200 students, in their own facilities, over the next two years. Additionally, using data collected in the evaluation process, I created a set of promotional materials that the school can use to generate future funding opportunities and create new partnerships. Both deliverables went through several rounds of feedback with my project partner.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
